!Act 2: The Bulwarks

Districts 3 and 4 under the Bleached Coral Colossus. Sabelle builds the Power Washer in the Wilds, Castella returns with the Colossus plan, and Gerold calls in at the Midpoint.

<<set $act to 2>>

!!Plot beats
//Length: 1.5 hours. Intensity: medium. Difficulty: medium.//
* ''First Pinch Point:'' Slum-like District 3 and run-down District 4 are badly Bleached. A Bleached Coral Colossus roams with smaller coral creatures it keeps seeding, spreading the Bleaching and wrecking property. The MC can't fight it yet and has to sneak past.
* ''Midpoint:'' The MC earns the trust of the locals (Omelia, Polyp, Pearl, Dench and his Citizen Watch, one of whom is paid by the King) and follows Sir Richard's trail. A second research station points to a cover-up: powerful Atlanteans and Council members profit from trading Coraltech for surface steampunk tech, while fossil-fuel pollution grows and most deny it. Sir Richard's notes show he warned both the Council and the King and was ignored; some notes are encrypted with no cipher. On the radio, liaison Gerold denies any warning reached the surface and suggests Sir Richard was delusional.
* ''Sir Richard's theory:'' He came to believe the Leviathan, worshipped as a god, causes the Bleaching to punish both peoples for their pollution. Rebuffed on all sides, he set out to hunt it down to buy time for environmental reform.
* ''The Power Washer:'' The MC gathers parts from both districts and brings them to Sabelle in the Wilds (home to the coral farm cave, the only place the special coral for Coraltech grows, and a booming steampunk plant). Sabelle builds the Coraltech Power Washer.
* ''Colossus plan:'' Castella catches up and helps the MC talk both districts' representatives into a joint plan. Together they lure out and defeat the Colossus, showing what the city can do united. The MC commits to following Sir Richard's trail and finding out who tried to silence his pollution theory.

